# Authelia SSO alerts.
#
# Scope: liveness. Authelia is the forward-auth gate for the *arr and file UIs
# (traefik_services `auth: true` → the `authelia` forwardAuth middleware). Traefik
# calls its authz endpoint on EVERY request to a gated service, so if Authelia is
# down those services fail at the gate (502/deny) even though their own containers
# are perfectly healthy — an outage that looks like "sonarr is broken" while sonarr
# is fine. That makes Authelia load-bearing and its liveness non-optional to
# observe (silent failure is the same severity class as loud failure).
#
# Datasource: VictoriaMetrics (PromQL). Source: the `authelia` vmagent scrape job
# (up{job="authelia"}) against 127.0.0.1:9959/metrics (telemetry.metrics in the
# authelia role config; loopback-published, never LAN-exposed).
#
# Quoting: any annotation surfacing $value/printf uses single-quoted-outer /
# escaped-inner per docs/conventions/vmalert-rule-quoting.md.

groups:
  - name: authelia
    interval: 1m
    rules:

      # ── Authelia liveness (container down OR scrape failing) ──────────
      - alert: AutheliaDown
        expr: up{job="authelia"} == 0
        for: {{ vmalert_authelia_down_for | default('5m') }}
        labels:
          severity: crit
        annotations:
          summary: "Authelia SSO is down — gated services are unreachable"
          description: >-
            The authelia scrape target has been down for
            {{ vmalert_authelia_down_for | default('5m') }}. Traefik calls
            Authelia's authz endpoint on every request to a forward-auth'd
            service, so the gated UIs are failing at the gate right now even
            though their own containers may be healthy. Check
            `docker logs authelia` and its Postgres backend (it stores sessions
            in the `authelia` DB on the shared postgresql container — a Postgres
            outage takes Authelia with it). Break-glass: reach the services on
            their LAN host ports (e.g. sonarr :8989, radarr :7878), which bypass
            Traefik and the gate entirely.
